  "question": {
    "text": "If <math><mi>p</mi></math>: <strong>A man is happy</strong> and&nbsp;<math><mi>q</mi></math>: <strong>A man is rich</strong> are two statements, then the statement, <strong>\"If a man is not happy, then he is not rich\"</strong>&nbsp;can be written using logical operators as"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mo>∼</mo> <mtext>p</mtext> <mo>→&nbsp;</mo> <mo>∼</mo> <mtext>q</mtext> </mrow> </math>",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mo>&sim;</mo> <mtext>q</mtext> <mo>&rarr;</mo> <mtext>p</mtext> </mrow> </math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mo>&sim;</mo> <mtext>q</mtext> <mo>&rarr;&nbsp;</mo> <mo>&sim;</mo> <mtext>p</mtext> </mrow> </math>",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "<math> <mrow> <mtext>q</mtext> <mo>&rarr;&nbsp;</mo> <mo>&sim;</mo> <mtext>p</mtext> </mrow> </math>",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "A"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Given,&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>p</mi><mo>:</mo></math>&nbsp;A man is happy&nbsp;</p><p>​and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>q</mi><mo>:</mo></math> A man is rich.<br /><br />&#39;If man is not happy, then he is not rich&#39; is written as&nbsp;<math> <mrow> <mo>&#8764;</mo> <mtext>p</mtext> <mo>&#8594;&#160;</mo> <mo>&#8764;</mo> <mtext>q</mtext> </mrow> </math></p>"
  }
